# join without on (DS0122); the right table is the last thing before the pipe.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | join u | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..25
  PIPELINE@0..24
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    JOIN_OP@9..15
      IDENT@9..13 "join"
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      NAME_REF@14..15
        IDENT@14..15 "u"
    WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
    PIPE@16..17 "|"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    TAKE_OP@18..24
      IDENT@18..22 "take"
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      LITERAL@23..24
        LONG@23..24 "1"
  WHITESPACE@24..25 "\n"

error[DS0122]: `join` needs `on` and the columns to match
  --> query:1:15
  |
1 | from t | join u | take 1
  |               ^ expected `on` after this table
  |
  = help: say which columns to match: `join u on customerId`
